Figure 7D, an immunoblot, verifies that Nano-11 induces the secretion of the active 17 kD form of IL-1β by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells. In the supernatant, the active 15 kD IL-1β is prominently observed when cells are stimulated with Nano-11, especially after LPS priming. Concurrently, the cell lysate shows the 30 kD biologically inactive pro-IL-1β, primarily in LPS-primed cells, indicating its intracellular production prior to cleavage and secretion. This confirms that Nano-11's ability to activate dendritic cells involves the generation and release of active, pro-inflammatory IL-1β, contributing to its adjuvant effect.